-- title:
--   Y-chart evaluation sends chart generators to coordinates of [0:1:0]
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, with associated projective Weierstrass cubic $W.\mathrm{toProjective}$ in $R[X_0,X_1,X_2] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R`. Write $\mathrm{mk}_3$ for the quotient map onto `ProjModelRingCR W.toProjective`, the quotient by the homogeneous ideal `projModelHomogeneousIdealCR` generated by that cubic, graded by `projModelGradingCR`, and let $\mathcal A_1$ be the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `HomogeneousLocalization.Away` of this graded ring at $\mathrm{mk}_3(X_1)$, i.e. the coordinate ring of the standard affine chart $X_1 \neq 0$. The ring homomorphism `kwYEvalRingHom` is evaluation of polynomials at the triple $(0,1,0)$, descended to `ProjModelRingCR W.toProjective` because the Weierstrass cubic vanishes at $(0,1,0)$; `kwYChartEval` is the induced homomorphism $\mathcal A_1 \to R$, obtained by mapping $\mathcal A_1$ into the localisation away from $\mathrm{mk}_3(X_1)$ and then applying the universal property, legitimate since $\mathrm{mk}_3(X_1)$ evaluates to the unit $1$. The assertion is that for every $m \in \{0,1,2\}$ the generator `kw_lrChart_gen W 1 m`, namely the degree-zero fraction $\mathrm{mk}_3(X_m)/\mathrm{mk}_3(X_1)$ of $\mathcal A_1$, is sent by `kwYChartEval` to the $m$-th entry of $(0,1,0)$, that is to $0$, $1$, $0$ respectively.
--
--   This is the evaluation of the $Y$-chart coordinate ring of the projective Weierstrass model at the point at infinity $[0:1:0]$, computed on the chart generators $X_m/X_1$. It is used in the treatment of the group law on the projective model, in particular by the results on factoring point evaluations through the standard charts and on independence of the chart factorisation of a point class.
